7.3
Failure Analysis
Trace inspection exposes three recurring failure types in end-to-
end workflows. First, scientific outcome failures occur after genuine
execution: indexing often produces inaccurate cells or HKL assign-
ments despite passing the gate, while refinement may improve fit
statistics without a valid structural result. Second, execution and ev-
idence failures prevent scoring or completion: 46 of 340 runs (13.5%)
fail at least one execution or physical gate, while 117 (34.4%) fail
